.TH env_addmodif 3
.SH NAME
env_addmodif \- append an environment-style key-value pair to a stralloc
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>
.br
.B #include <stralloc.h>

.B int env_addmodif(stralloc* \fIsa\fP, const char* \fIs\fP, const char* \fIt\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_addmodif
appends the string \fIs\fP followed by an optional "=" and string \fIt\fP 
to the stralloc \fIsa\fP. The resulting string is null-terminated 
within the stralloc.

If \fIt\fP is non-NULL, the function appends "=" and then the content 
of \fIt\fP. If \fIs\fP is NULL, the function returns 1 without modifying \fIsa\fP.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 if successful, 0 if memory allocation failed, in which case \fIsa\fP 
remains unchanged.